  "query_preview": "../Monday through Thursday/...A more active pattern\ncontinues into next week as a low redevelops in the Gulf Monday\ninto Tuesday, with continued onshore flow between waves of \nprecipitation through early to midweek. Once the low redevelops,\nit will bring another more organized band of precipitation\nthrough Tuesday followed by a few less organized waves Wednesday\ninto Thursday. The confidence on this midweek low looks to be a \nbit more aligned today between models, with the more organized low\ncenter location and main precipitation band moving through \nTuesday. Some uncertainty still remains on timing and rainfall \namounts, especially due to the more showery regime expected\nmidweek and spread on the low's track. The low also becomes more \npoorly formed and uncertain Wednesday onwards, as some solutions\nkeep it stronger for longer and moving towards the panhandle while\nothers have it falling apart further offshore or just south of the\npanhandle. Generally though, rainy conditions and elevated winds \nare expected to continue through midweek, only beginning to \ndiminish by late week as this low begins to fall apart.\n\nThe convective potential remains for Monday along the coast,\nkeeping the chance for thunderstorms developing over the waters\nand pushing into the outer coastline through the day, gradually\nshifting southward as the day goes on before diminishing into the\nnight.",
